# Next.js 15 & React 19 Guidelines

## Next.js 15 App Router
- Use Server Components by default, Client Components only when necessary
- Use `"use client"` directive only when needed for interactivity
- Leverage Next.js 15 App Router features (metadata, layouts, etc.)
- Use Next.js `Image` component for all images with proper `alt` attributes
- Use Next.js `Link` component for internal navigation
- Export metadata from page components for SEO

## React 19 Modern Features
- Use functional components with TypeScript
- Export as default for page components
- Use proper TypeScript interfaces for props
- Leverage modern React patterns and hooks
- Prefer composition over inheritance

## Component Structure
```tsx
export default function PageName() {
  return (
    <div className="min-h-screen">
      <section className="bg-[color]-50 py-16">
        <div className="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
          {/* Content */}
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Performance
- Use Next.js Image optimization
- Implement proper loading states
- Optimize for Core Web Vitals
- Use appropriate `priority` prop for above-the-fold images